  "notes": "The tail end of this lane and the door into the 2010s: 118–132 straight with the backbeat on 2&4. Two facts make this model its own thing. First, the 2008 breakout is notated in **12/8** — \"a compound-swing feel over a straight backbeat\" — which is the only reason `swing` moves at all here; it sits at 0.62, a heavy shuffle rather than a full triplet, because the research is explicit that the backbeat stays straight. Second, the harmony is given in full: verses Am–B°–C–Dm7–F5–Em and chorus Am–C–Dm–F–Em, with a bridge of F–Em–Am–G — note the diminished passing chord and the **minor v instead of a dominant**, both of which are authored as degrees (`ii°` and `v`) with `maxChords` raised to 6. Three drum deltas come from the \"throbbing glam-rock beat\": \"kick on all four in the chorus\", \"handclap-reinforced snare on 2&4\", and \"8th hat with an open hat on 4&\" plus \"tom-driven fills into choruses\", which is the tom-led perc block. The bass is \"fat mono synth bass in 8ths with an octave-jump figure\", so the octave is its passing tone. The melody is documented as A3–E5 with \"a chanted 2-bar hook repeated four times\". ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are `swing.amount` 0.62 — the reading of \"compound-swing over a straight backbeat\" — and every drum probability.",
